X
XFor each interface, a predefined field of the environment variable
Xmay be set.  For the ascii interface, the _ASCII (user-defined) is
Xfollowed by 16 characters representing ascii keyboard controls.
XEach interface may have a custom handler that passes internal parameters.
XFor example, the X interface may put it's variables between '[' and ']'.
XThese are defined by a module which deals with the parameters.
X
Xsetenv MGT="_ASCII=q><.,ebcx][gnpui@O.+ _XTERM=[24x32,gterm=white...] _MAC="
X                                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ ^^^^^^
X                                        (not yet defined  . . . . . . . . . )
X
X
XOne way to activate the environmental variable 'MGT' is to stipulate the
Xequate  ('setenv ....' line above)  in your .login or .cshrc file.
XAlternatively, you can simply type a variant line at your terminal if you
Xwish to change the ascii equates of the local environmental setting. 
XSay that you wish to display the Black stones as an "*" instead of a "@":
X   simply substitute a "*" for "@" in the  'setenv MGT ... '  equate line.
XTo display the GO-board star points as "," instead of "+" follow a similar
X   procedure.
X  
X
XIf you don't do anything, the program uses its default, as displayed above.
