XCOMMANDS:
XThe commands are listed to the right of "Commands".  In order, they are:
X
X'q': Quit: quit.  Will verify, type 'y' or 'n'.
X'>': Move Forward: Continue forward, but stop at end of variation.
X'<': Move Backward: Continue backward, but stop at beginning of file
X		and do not visit other variations.
X'.': Move Forward: visit other variations.  This is the usual command for
X		examining the data.
X',': Move Backward: visit other variations.  This visits the information in
X		the reverse order as the 'Move Forward' command.
X'e': End (Go to End): Go to the end of the current variation.
X'b': Beginning (Go to Beginning): Go to the beginning/front of all variations.
X'c': Move Forward To Comment: Like the previous command, but don't stop
X		until you hit a comment.
X'x': Move Backward To Comment: like the previous command, but don't stop
X		until you hit a comment.
X']': Move Forward to Choice:  Move forward until you come to the point where
X		there is a choice.
X'[': Move Backward to Choice:  Move Backward until you come to the point where
X		there is a choice.
X'g': Goto Node Number:  type in a node number and mgt will display that node.
X'n': Display Comment Below (scroll down):  If you see a '+' near the bottom
X		of the comment, there is more comment to be displayed.
X		'p' will scroll the comment down.
X'p': Display Comment Above (scroll up):  If you see a '-', there is more
X		comment to be seen above.  This will scroll up.
X'i': Display Choices Below (scroll down):  Like 'j' for choices.
X'u': Display Choices Above (scroll up):  Like 'k' for choices.
